8. REQUIREMENTS VALIDATION
===================================================

- Demonstrates that requirements define the system the customer
  really wants.
- Very important — error costs are high:
  >>> Fixing a requirements error after delivery may cost up
      to 100 TIMES the cost of fixing an implementation error.

CHECKS DURING VALIDATION
  - Validity: Does the system provide functions that best
    support the customer's needs?
  - Consistency: Are there any requirement conflicts?
  - Completeness: Are all customer-required functions included?
  - Realism: Can requirements be implemented given budget/tech?
  - Verifiability: Can the requirements actually be checked?

VALIDATION TECHNIQUES
  - Requirements reviews: systematic manual analysis.
  - Prototyping: use an executable model to check requirements.
  - Test-case generation: develop tests to check testability.

REQUIREMENTS REVIEWS
  - Should be held regularly while requirements are being
    formulated.
  - Both client AND contractor staff should participate.
  - Can be formal (with completed docs) or informal — good
    communication resolves problems early.

REVIEW CHECKS
  - Verifiability: Is the requirement realistically testable?
  - Comprehensibility: Is it properly understood?
  - Traceability: Is its origin clearly stated?
  - Adaptability: Can it be changed without major impact on
    other requirements?


